# Thoughts routing

When the user invokes Thoughts to assess an idea, asks for an honest opinion, or
challenges your reasoning, read `~/.cursor/skills/thoughts/SKILL.md` and follow its
Activation section. The skill is authoritative for review mode, council execution,
evidence requirements, fallback behavior, and the response receipt.

Treat a quoted trigger or discussion of the skill as task content, not an automatic
council invocation. Honor explicit user choices such as "no council" or "full
council" as directed by the skill. This rule does not duplicate its procedure.
